<title>MALAYSIA: Telekom, SBC eye SAfrica's Telkom.</title>
<headline>Telekom, SBC eye SAfrica's Telkom.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telekom Malaysia Bhd said it had signed an agreement with US-based SBC Communications Inc to pursue a stake in South Africa's Telkom SA Ltd, which plans to divest up to 30 percent of its shares.</p>
<p>Both Telekom, Malaysia's national telephone company, and SBC, a wireless communications firm, have been shortlisted for the South African government's planned sale of up to 30 percent of the capital in Telkom, a Telekom Malaysia statement said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The statement to the KLSE added that the statement formalised the cooperative effort between the two parties, announced by South African Post, Telecommunications and Broadcasting Minister Jay Naidoo in November.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-2307509)</p>
